{"step_index":113,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T11:03:31Z","thinking":"The `test_api.py` file defines a `run_tests()` function, which suggests it might contain test logic. Django's test runner typically executes subclasses of `unittest.TestCase`, and this file doesn't inherit from that class. Therefore, it's not automatically run as part of the standard test suite. Examining Phase 1 and Phase 2 is the next step.\n\n\nThe `AIChatView`'s current implementation retrieves only a limited set of recent books. The goal is to enhance this by building a comprehensive knowledge base for all books. This involves retrieving full catalog statistics and metadata, including the total book count, audiobook count, unique genres and authors, and a comprehensive list of all book details. This expanded data will provide a solid base for improved Q&A capabilities.\n\n\nThe library statistics and book list provide a foundation for answering quantitative and factual questions directly. For specific book inquiries, a search across titles, authors, and content summaries is the best approach to find relevant details. If no Gemini API key is configured, the system can parse the library statistics to answer basic questions such as total book count or lists of audiobooks and genres.\n\n\nThe system now incorporates a fallback mechanism: if the external API request fails, it leverages local knowledge to provide an answer. Analyzing Phase 3 indicates the requirement to update the database schema by adding fields for audio file or URL within the `Book` model, which has been done.\n\n\nThe `Book` model will be updated with `audio_file` and `audiobook_url` fields to support both direct uploads and external links. A `get_audio_url` method is proposed for retrieving the correct audio URL based on available fields. The `BookSerializer` in `core/serializers.py` will be updated to include these new fields, handle absolute URLs, and include a `has_audio` boolean. An `AudioUploadSerializer` is also required to validate audio file formats. The `BookViewSet` will have `IsAdminOrReadOnly` permissions. The book upload will allow both PDF and audio files.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Surface PC\\\\.gemini\\\\core\\\\models.py\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing core/models.py\"","toolSummary":"\"View core/models.py\""}}]}
